# Copy to .env and edit. Only WORKER is required.

# ssh destination of the second Spark (rank 1). Passwordless ssh, and its user
# can run docker. Its address on the direct cable makes the one-time copy of
# the ~207 GB of weights much faster.
WORKER=you@192.0.2.2

# Where the weights and the converted overlay live (~223 GB). The same absolute
# path is used on both Sparks. Default: $HOME/models/sparkglm
#MODEL_ROOT=/srv/models/sparkglm

# 4x512k (default): 4 requests x 512K context. 8x128k: 8 requests x 128K.
#PROFILE=4x512k

# Share of each Spark's unified memory for the engine (0.80-0.95, default 0.88).
# On Sparks that run nothing else, 0.91 roughly doubles the KV pool that holds
# long contexts and the prefix cache (about 600K to 1.13M tokens). Above 0.91,
# real traffic took our rank 0 below 1 GiB free; keep at least ~4 GB free.
#GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.91

# Keep conversations that fall out of the prefix cache on each Spark's own disk
# (ext4/xfs, not tmpfs), so a returning conversation is read back instead of
# prefilled again. Off unless the directory is set. It is created at the same
# path on both Sparks. The size is in GiB per Spark (16-100, default 48) and
# must be free there; the default takes about 60K tokens from the KV pool.
#PREFIX_CACHE_DIR=/srv/sparkglm/prefix-cache
#PREFIX_CACHE_GB=48

# Lend each Spark's 2 GiB display carveout (GB10 firmware memory that Linux
# never sees) to the KV cache. The containers then start with CAP_SYS_ADMIN to
# export it, which the server drops before it loads anything, and share
# /run/lock/sparkglm. Default off; set 0 or delete the line to roll back.
#DISPLAY_CARVEOUT=1

# Build the image from source instead of pulling ghcr.io/enntity/atlas-sparkglm.
#BUILD=1
# Parallel compile jobs for a source build; lower it if the build runs out of memory.
#ATLAS_BUILD_JOBS=4

# Only for private Hugging Face mirrors; the pinned checkpoints are public.
#HF_TOKEN=

# Detected from the RoCE device; set only if detection picks the wrong port.
#FABRIC_HCA=rocep1s0f0
#FABRIC_INTERFACE=enp1s0f0np0
# The fabric also uses the RDMA device behind the ConnectX-7's other PCIe domain
# (same cable on a DGX Spark). Set 0 on boards that wire it to a second physical
# port with no cable to the other Spark (ASUS GX10).
#FABRIC_SIBLINGS=0
#LEADER_ADDRESS=192.0.2.1
